# The Windows installer IS served from this site, so it must NOT be excluded.
# Earlier releases moved it to GitHub on the mistaken belief that its ~99 MB
# size caused "File size limit exceeded". The real cause was src-tauri/target
# below; with that excluded the installer uploads fine.
# Superseded Tauri installers stay out — only the one latest.json references
# needs to ship.

# Build output that must never reach the deploy payload.
# src-tauri/target is 5.7 GB of Rust artifacts and contains individual .rlib
# files over 100 MB, which Vercel rejects outright. This was the real cause of
# "File size limit exceeded" — it appeared after the Tauri migration started
# and nothing excluded it.
